From e91ce746c96abb8736dea5a12a74c65118338a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:51:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] feat(control-plane): count instance checks, redeploys
 and reclaims

The runtime health work checks deployed instances at startup and
periodically, redeploys services whose instance is gone with a backoff
and reclaims allocations whose owner no longer exists, but none of it
showed up in /metrics: how often instances are lost, whether the
periodic check keeps failing or whether orphaned allocations cannot be
reclaimed could only be read from the logs.

Add four counters with fixed enum labels only, every label combination
starting at zero:

- forgemesh_instance_checks_total{outcome}: periodic checks by the
  controller, completed or failed (the startup check is not counted,
  the control plane does not start when it fails);
- forgemesh_instance_check_results_total{check,result}: services a
  check reached a result for (lost, back or conflict), at startup or
  periodically;
- forgemesh_lost_instance_redeploys_total: redeployment runs started
  for services whose instance is gone; rounds deferred by the backoff
  are not counted;
- forgemesh_orphaned_allocation_reclaims_total{outcome}: reclaimed, or
  failed and kept for the next resync.

check_instances and reclaim_orphaned_allocations report through a new
keyword-only on_result callback and ReconciliationController takes an
on_redeploy callback, so the deployment and reconciler modules stay
free of metrics; the app wires them to ControllerMetrics. Nothing
changes when the callbacks are not given.
